<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  WreckedMachines — the RR "Analyse" study→unlock loop, WRECKED_MACHINES_
  RESURRECTION_1.

  This is DESIGN.md §2's own worked example (owner-ratified 2026-08-12 — "the
  wreck is the main way to learn"), re-enabled rather than newly invented.
  V2.md §8 named it as deferred-not-cancelled, and the mechanism it deferred
  was already verified against files on disk (not just remembered): RR ships
  its own use case (RR_autodoor, Door -> Autodoors) in
  v1.6/Defs/Specials/SpecialResearchOpportunities_Core.xml, all ten
  SpecialResearchOpportunityDef fields confirmed via `strings` on the shipped
  ResearchReinvented.dll, and Analyse (not AnalyseProductionFacility) is the
  right opportunityType because its picker,
  JobPicker_AnalyseInPlaceOrMinified, lets a pawn study a thing WHERE IT
  STANDS — the only behaviour an immovable wreck can support.
  AnalyseProductionFacility needs a pawn WORKING AT the building
  (JobPicker_NoJob) and is wrong for a wreck that has no work to give.

  petetimessix.researchreinvented — confirmed ACTIVE, live ModsConfig.xml,
  checked this session (also confirmed by TECHPRINT_FACTION_GATING_1 the same
  night). MayRequire guards the def anyway in case a future minimal mod list
  drops it for a quicktest.

  `project` now points at RM_WM_AutomatedSmelterRestoration (this mod's own
  Ship-tree project, ResearchProjects_WreckedMachines.xml) rather than
  VFE_BasicFactories — the re-pointing WRECKED_MACHINES_RESURRECTION_1 made,
  so studying the wreck credits the gate that actually unlocks OUR repaired
  tier, not the untouched donor building's vanilla research.

  ⚠️ NOT VERIFIED AT RUNTIME — reserved for the owner's own quicktest, not
  attempted here (see infrastructure/state/items/
  WRECKED_MACHINES_RESURRECTION_1.md "verify"):
    1. That this opportunity actually surfaces in the research UI for a
       colonist to take.
    2. `targetIterations 5.0` under RR's default ReverseEngineering category
       preset (DESIGN.md §2) — whether five study sessions feels right in
       play is untested; the importanceMultiplier below is the first dial to
       reach for if it needs retuning, since it is scoped to this def alone.
    3. The bigger open question this whole mod rides on: whether the
       `replaceTags` build-over (both tiers share WM_AutomatedSmelter) still
       places correctly with Replace Stuff - Continued active, given its
       Harmony postfix forces CanReplace false for any
       IsNonDeconstructibleAttackableBuilding (DESIGN.md §4). It does NOT
       apply here directly — v1's tiers ship deconstructible=true, so the
       postfix's non-deconstructible condition never triggers — but confirm
       this def's Analyse target (RM_WM_AutomatedSmelter_Wrecked) still
       exists on the map to be studied AFTER a kludged/repaired build-over
       has replaced it; if the wreck is gone, the opportunity has nothing
       left to point at.
-->
<Defs>

  <PeteTimesSix.ResearchReinvented.Defs.SpecialResearchOpportunityDef
      ParentName="SpecialResearchOpportunityBase" MayRequire="petetimessix.researchreinvented">
    <defName>RM_WM_AnalyseWreckedSmelter</defName>
    <opportunityType>Analyse</opportunityType>
    <project>RM_WM_AutomatedSmelterRestoration</project>
    <things>
      <li>RM_WM_AutomatedSmelter_Wrecked</li>
    </things>
  </PeteTimesSix.ResearchReinvented.Defs.SpecialResearchOpportunityDef>

</Defs>
